---
// src/pages/en/interactive-lessons.astro
// Interactive Lessons: Guided Active Learning with Micro-Widgets and Socratic Copilot
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import { appLink } from "@colabedu/ui-core/navigation";
import "../../styles/global.css";

const catalogUrl = appLink('app', '/navigator/spec_root/0');
const seoCatalogUrl = appLink('catalog', '/');
const appUrl = appLink('app', '/');
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="scroll-smooth">
<head>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="alternate icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Interactive Lessons: Guided Active Learning | ColabEdu.net</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Discover ColabEdu Interactive Lessons: structured slide-based micro-learning featuring KaTeX formulas, dynamic simulations, Socratic checkpoints, and virtual labs that surpass static PDFs.">
    
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800;900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css" rel="stylesheet">

    <style is:global>
        :root {
            --font-sans: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;
            --font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
        }
        body {
            font-family: var(--font-sans);
            background-color: #FAF9F6;
            color: #0F172A;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        }
        .precision-card {
            background-color: #FFFFFF;
            border: 1px solid #E2E8F0;
            border-radius: 1.25rem;
            box-shadow: 0 1px 3px 0 rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.03);
            transition: all 0.2s ease-in-out;
        }
        .precision-card:hover {
            border-color: #CBD5E1;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 20px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
        }
        .hero-lessons {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(238, 242, 255, 0.7) 0%, rgba(224, 231, 255, 0.5) 50%, rgba(240, 253, 250, 0.4) 100%);
            border: 1px solid rgba(226, 232, 240, 0.8);
            border-radius: 2rem;
        }
        .lesson-canvas-container {
            background: #0F172A;
            border-radius: 1rem;
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        /* Alternating chromatic background rhythm */
        .section-tint-blue {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #FFFFFF 0%, rgba(239, 246, 255, 0.45) 100%);
            border: 1px solid #BFDBFE;
        }
        .section-tint-teal {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #FFFFFF 0%, rgba(204, 251, 241, 0.45) 100%);
            border: 1px solid #99F6E4;
        }
        .section-tint-indigo {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #FFFFFF 0%, rgba(238, 242, 255, 0.5) 100%);
            border: 1px solid #C7D2FE;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="selection:bg-blue-600 selection:text-white">

    <Header lang="en" />

    <main class="py-12 sm:py-16">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
            
            <!-- Hero Title -->
            <div class="hero-lessons p-8 sm:p-14 text-center mb-16">
                <span class="inline-block text-xs font-mono font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-blue-900 bg-white/80 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-blue-300 mb-6">
                    <i class="fas fa-layer-group mr-1.5 text-blue-600"></i> Active Pedagogy & Socratic Scaffolding
                </span>
                <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-black text-slate-950 tracking-tight leading-tight mb-6">
                    The end of the static PDF.<br/>
                    Lessons that come alive.
                </h1>
                <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8">
                    We transform official syllabi into guided micro-learning experiences. Every lesson unites curricular rigor, dynamic mathematical visualization, interactive simulators, and Socratic reflection checkpoints.
                </p>
                
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
                    <a href="#demo-interactive" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-md hover:bg-blue-700 transition flex items-center gap-2">
                        <i class="fas fa-play text-xs"></i>
                        <span>Try Lesson Simulator</span>
                    </a>
                    <a href={catalogUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-white text-slate-800 font-bold text-sm border border-slate-300 hover:bg-slate-50 transition flex items-center gap-2">
                        <i class="fas fa-book-open text-blue-600"></i>
                        <span>Explore Lessons in Catalog</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- What is an Interactive Lesson? (3 Pedagogical Principles) -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-16">
                <div class="precision-card p-6">
                    <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg mb-4">
                        <i class="fas fa-shoe-prints"></i>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-blue-700 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Progressive Scaffolding</span>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-black text-slate-900 mb-2">Optimal Cognitive Load Slides</h3>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Instead of overwhelming 30-page chapters, content is organized into a canonical sequence of 4 to 9 slides: hook, core concept, hands-on simulation, and synthesis.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="precision-card p-6">
                    <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg mb-4">
                        <i class="fas fa-sliders"></i>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-teal-700 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Conceptual Manipulation</span>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-black text-slate-900 mb-2">Learn by Adjusting Variables</h3>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Students don't memorize abstract formulas; they adjust velocity sliders, angle inputs, or chemical parameters to immediately observe effects in real time.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="precision-card p-6">
                    <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg mb-4">
                        <i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-indigo-700 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Socratic Checkpoints</span>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-black text-slate-900 mb-2">Verification Without Easy Answers</h3>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Built-in checkpoints test comprehension. If a student errs, they receive a targeted Socratic hint guiding their deduction rather than a spoon-fed answer.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- LIVE DEMO SECTION: LESSON SIMULATOR -->
            <div id="demo-interactive" class="precision-card section-tint-blue p-6 sm:p-10 mb-16 shadow-lg border-blue-200 scroll-mt-24">
                
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200 mb-8">
                    <div>
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-blue-600 uppercase tracking-widest block mb-1">
                            <i class="fas fa-desktop mr-1.5"></i> A2UI Classroom Demo
                        </span>
                        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-950">
                            High School Physics: Projectile Motion Kinematics
                        </h2>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 bg-slate-100 p-1.5 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-slate-600">
                        <span id="slide-indicator">Step 1 of 4</span>
                        <span class="text-slate-300">|</span>
                        <span class="text-emerald-700 font-bold"><i class="fas fa-circle text-[8px] mr-1"></i>Live</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- LESSON WIDGET CONTAINER -->
                <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 min-h-[440px] flex flex-col justify-between">
                    
                    <!-- STEP 1: HOOK AND MOTIVATION -->
                    <div id="lesson-step-1" class="lesson-step">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold font-mono text-indigo-700 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">
                            <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md bg-indigo-100">Step 1 · The Real-World Problem</span>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-4">
                            Why does a projectile achieve maximum range at 45°?
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                            Think of a penalty kick in soccer, a firefighting water cannon, or a space rover landing. Parabolic motion results from two simultaneous, independent orthogonal motions formulated by Galileo Galilei in 1638:
                        </p>
                        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
                            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
                                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-blue-700 uppercase block mb-1">Horizontal Axis (X)</span>
                                <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Uniform Rectilinear Motion. Horizontal velocity remains constant because no horizontal acceleration acts in a vacuum:</p>
                                <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 bg-slate-50 p-2 rounded">
                                    v_x = v_0 · cos(&alpha;)
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
                                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-teal-700 uppercase block mb-1">Vertical Axis (Y)</span>
                                <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Uniformly Accelerated Motion, governed continuously by planetary gravitational pull:</p>
                                <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 bg-slate-50 p-2 rounded">
                                    v_y = v_0 · sin(&alpha;) - g · t
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- STEP 2: INTERACTIVE CANVAS WITH SLIDERS -->
                    <div id="lesson-step-2" class="lesson-step hidden">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold font-mono text-teal-700 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">
                            <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md bg-teal-100">Step 2 · Hands-on Virtual Lab</span>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-2">
                            Simulate the Trajectory in Real Time
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">
                            Adjust angle and initial velocity. Observe how the curve bends and the maximum horizontal range X_max changes:
                        </p>

                        <!-- Canvas and Controls -->
                        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4">
                            <!-- Canvas Visualizer -->
                            <div class="lg:col-span-2 lesson-canvas-container p-3 flex flex-col justify-between h-56 sm:h-64">
                                <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
                                    <span>Cartesian Plane (x, y)</span>
                                    <span id="telemetry-info" class="text-emerald-400 font-bold">Range: 40.8 m | Max Height: 10.2 m</span>
                                </div>
                                <canvas id="trajectory-canvas" class="w-full h-44"></canvas>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Interactive Sliders -->
                            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 flex flex-col justify-around">
                                <div>
                                    <div class="flex justify-between text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 mb-1">
                                        <span>Launch Angle (&alpha;):</span>
                                        <span id="angle-display" class="font-mono text-blue-600 font-black">45°</span>
                                    </div>
                                    <input type="range" id="angle-slider" min="15" max="80" value="45" step="1" class="w-full h-2 bg-slate-200 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-blue-600">
                                    <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] text-slate-400 font-mono mt-1">
                                        <span>15° (flat)</span>
                                        <span>45° (optimal)</span>
                                        <span>80° (vertical)</span>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="mt-4">
                                    <div class="flex justify-between text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 mb-1">
                                        <span>Initial Velocity (v_0):</span>
                                        <span id="velocity-display" class="font-mono text-teal-600 font-black">20 m/s</span>
                                    </div>
                                    <input type="range" id="velocity-slider" min="10" max="35" value="20" step="1" class="w-full h-2 bg-slate-200 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-teal-600">
                                    <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] text-slate-400 font-mono mt-1">
                                        <span>10 m/s</span>
                                        <span>35 m/s</span>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="mt-3 p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-[11px] text-slate-600 font-mono">
                                    Canonical Formula: <span class="font-bold text-slate-800">X_max = (v_0² · sin(2&alpha;)) / g</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- STEP 3: SOCRATIC COMPREHENSION CHECKPOINT -->
                    <div id="lesson-step-3" class="lesson-step hidden">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold font-mono text-amber-700 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">
                            <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md bg-amber-100">Step 3 · Conceptual Reasoning Checkpoint</span>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-2">
                            The Dilemma of 30° and 60°
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mb-6">
                            You fire two projectiles with identical initial speed: one at 30° and another at 60°. Neglecting air resistance, which one achieves the greater horizontal distance?
                        </p>

                        <!-- Quiz Options -->
                        <div class="space-y-3 mb-6" id="quiz-options">
                            <button class="quiz-option w-full p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 hover:border-blue-400 hover:bg-blue-50/40 text-left transition text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 flex items-center justify-between" data-choice="30">
                                <span>A) The 30° launch, because it has less air time and travels faster horizontally.</span>
                                <i class="far fa-circle text-slate-300 choice-icon"></i>
                            </button>

                            <button class="quiz-option w-full p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 hover:border-blue-400 hover:bg-blue-50/40 text-left transition text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 flex items-center justify-between" data-choice="60">
                                <span>B) The 60° launch, because it stays aloft longer thanks to higher vertical lift.</span>
                                <i class="far fa-circle text-slate-300 choice-icon"></i>
                            </button>

                            <button class="quiz-option w-full p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 hover:border-blue-400 hover:bg-blue-50/40 text-left transition text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 flex items-center justify-between" data-choice="equal">
                                <span>C) Both reach exactly the same horizontal distance (X_max).</span>
                                <i class="far fa-circle text-slate-300 choice-icon"></i>
                            </button>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Socratic Feedback Box -->
                        <div id="quiz-feedback" class="hidden p-4 rounded-xl border text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            <!-- Injected dynamically -->
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- STEP 4: SYNTHESIS AND CONCLUSION -->
                    <div id="lesson-step-4" class="lesson-step hidden">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold font-mono text-emerald-700 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">
                            <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md bg-emerald-100">Step 4 · Learning Synthesis</span>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-4">
                            Concept Successfully Mastered!
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                            You have proven experimentally and analytically the principle of <strong>complementary launch angles</strong> in kinematics: any angle pair summing to 90° (30° + 60° = 90°) yields the exact same horizontal range, because sin(2 · 30°) = sin(60°) = sin(120°) = sin(2 · 60°) = 0.866. One projectile travels high with low horizontal speed; the other skims flat but fast.
                        </p>
                        
                        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-200 text-xs text-emerald-900 mb-6">
                            <div class="font-bold flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
                                <i class="fas fa-check-circle text-emerald-600"></i>
                                <span>Curricular Standards Alignment:</span>
                            </div>
                            <p class="leading-relaxed">
                                AP Physics 1 Kinematics 2D & Next Generation Science Standards (NGSS HS-PS2-1: Forces and Motion).
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- NAVIGATION BOTTOM BAR -->
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 mt-6">
                        <button id="btn-prev" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 text-slate-600 font-bold text-xs hover:bg-slate-100 transition disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed flex items-center gap-2" disabled>
                            <i class="fas fa-chevron-left text-[10px]"></i>
                            <span>Previous</span>
                        </button>

                        <div class="flex gap-2" id="step-dots">
                            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-blue-600 dot-indicator"></span>
                            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-slate-300 dot-indicator"></span>
                            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-slate-300 dot-indicator"></span>
                            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-slate-300 dot-indicator"></span>
                        </div>

                        <button id="btn-next" class="px-5 py-2 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold text-xs shadow-xs hover:bg-blue-700 transition flex items-center gap-2">
                            <span>Next</span>
                            <i class="fas fa-chevron-right text-[10px]"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- A2UI MICRO-WIDGETS CATALOG -->
            <div class="precision-card section-tint-teal p-8 sm:p-12 mb-16 shadow-lg border-teal-200">
                <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
                    <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-teal-800 uppercase tracking-widest block mb-2">
                        A2UI Pedagogical Component Ecosystem
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
                        Ready-to-Use Learning Widgets
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-2">
                        Every lesson in ColabEdu is assembled using certified pedagogical widgets, without writing custom frontend code.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                    
                    <!-- Widget 1: KaTeX -->
                    <div class="precision-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
                        <div>
                            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-blue-50 text-blue-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-square-root-variable"></i>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base mb-1">KaTeX Formula Editor</h4>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                High-resolution mathematical typesetting. Ultra-fast rendering of matrices, calculus integrals, and limits.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="p-2.5 bg-slate-50 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 font-mono text-[11px] text-slate-700">
                            &int; f(x) dx = F(b) - F(a)
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Widget 2: PhET Labs -->
                    <div class="precision-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
                        <div>
                            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-teal-50 text-teal-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-flask"></i>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base mb-1">Embedded PhET Labs</h4>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                Seamless integration with University of Colorado virtual labs: electric circuits, stoichiometry, and optics.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="text-[11px] font-mono text-teal-700 bg-teal-50 p-2 rounded-lg border border-teal-200">
                            100% interactive · Zero Java plugins
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Widget 3: Sequencing & Matching -->
                    <div class="precision-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
                        <div>
                            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-bars-staggered"></i>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base mb-1">Sequencing & Matching</h4>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                Draggable tiles for ordering historical timelines, algorithm steps, or pairing definitions with formal terms.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="text-[11px] font-mono text-indigo-700 bg-indigo-50 p-2 rounded-lg border border-indigo-200">
                            Touch-optimized Drag & Drop
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Widget 4: Function Plotter -->
                    <div class="precision-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
                        <div>
                            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-purple-50 text-purple-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base mb-1">CAS Function Plotter</h4>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                Plots curves, asymptotes, and derivatives as students manipulate constants via dynamic sliders.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="text-[11px] font-mono text-purple-700 bg-purple-50 p-2 rounded-lg border border-purple-200">
                            Symja CAS · Infinitesimal precision
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Widget 5: Mermaid Diagrams -->
                    <div class="precision-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
                        <div>
                            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-project-diagram"></i>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base mb-1">Mermaid Concept Maps</h4>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                Family trees, biological pathways, and taxonomies that dynamically expand when tapping individual nodes.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="text-[11px] font-mono text-amber-700 bg-amber-50 p-2 rounded-lg border border-amber-200">
                            Native vector SVG
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Widget 6: Video Checkpoints -->
                    <div class="precision-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
                        <div>
                            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-rose-50 text-rose-600 flex items-center justify-center font-bold mb-4">
                                <i class="fas fa-circle-play"></i>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base mb-1">Video Socratic Stops</h4>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                Real laboratory clips that pause playback at the key moment to prompt an inductive student hypothesis.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="text-[11px] font-mono text-rose-700 bg-rose-50 p-2 rounded-lg border border-rose-200">
                            Active vs. passive viewing
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FINAL BANNER TO EXAMS AND CATALOG -->
            <div class="p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 to-indigo-950 text-white flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-8 shadow-xl">
                <div class="max-w-xl">
                    <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-blue-400 uppercase tracking-widest block mb-2">
                        Next Pedagogical Step
                    </span>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight mb-3">
                        How to evaluate lessons with official rigor?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                        Discover how ColabEdu evaluates scanned handwritten exams, voice recordings, and digital tests with official rubrics and sovereign teacher review.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 w-full md:w-auto shrink-0">
                    <a href="/en/interactive-exams" class="px-6 py-3.5 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold text-sm text-center shadow-md hover:bg-blue-500 transition">
                        Explore Interactive Exams &rarr;
                    </a>
                    <a href={catalogUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="px-6 py-3.5 rounded-xl bg-white/10 text-white font-bold text-sm text-center hover:bg-white/20 transition border border-white/20">
                        OER Catalog
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </main>

    <Footer lang="en" />

    <!-- LIVE DEMO REACTIVITY SCRIPT -->
    <script is:inline>
        let currentStep = 1;
        const totalSteps = 4;

        function updateStep(step) {
            currentStep = step;
            document.querySelectorAll('.lesson-step').forEach((el, idx) => {
                if (idx + 1 === currentStep) {
                    el.classList.remove('hidden');
                } else {
                    el.classList.add('hidden');
                }
            });

            const indicator = document.getElementById('slide-indicator');
            if (indicator) indicator.textContent = `Step ${currentStep} of ${totalSteps}`;

            const dots = document.querySelectorAll('.dot-indicator');
            dots.forEach((dot, idx) => {
                if (idx + 1 === currentStep) {
                    dot.className = 'w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-blue-600 dot-indicator';
                } else {
                    dot.className = 'w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-slate-300 dot-indicator';
                }
            });

            const btnPrev = document.getElementById('btn-prev');
            const btnNext = document.getElementById('btn-next');
            if (btnPrev) btnPrev.disabled = currentStep === 1;
            if (btnNext) {
                if (currentStep === totalSteps) {
                    btnNext.innerHTML = '<span>Restart</span> <i class="fas fa-rotate-right text-[10px]"></i>';
                } else {
                    btnNext.innerHTML = '<span>Next</span> <i class="fas fa-chevron-right text-[10px]"></i>';
                }
            }

            if (currentStep === 2) {
                setTimeout(drawTrajectory, 60);
            }
        }

        document.getElementById('btn-prev')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
            if (currentStep > 1) updateStep(currentStep - 1);
        });

        document.getElementById('btn-next')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
            if (currentStep < totalSteps) {
                updateStep(currentStep + 1);
            } else {
                updateStep(1);
            }
        });

        // CANVAS TRAJECTORY SIMULATION
        const canvas = document.getElementById('trajectory-canvas');
        const angleSlider = document.getElementById('angle-slider');
        const velocitySlider = document.getElementById('velocity-slider');
        const angleDisplay = document.getElementById('angle-display');
        const velocityDisplay = document.getElementById('velocity-display');
        const telemetry = document.getElementById('telemetry-info');

        function drawTrajectory() {
            if (!canvas) return;
            const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
            const width = canvas.clientWidth;
            const height = canvas.clientHeight;
            if (width === 0 || height === 0) return;
            canvas.width = width * (window.devicePixelRatio || 1);
            canvas.height = height * (window.devicePixelRatio || 1);
            ctx.scale(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, window.devicePixelRatio || 1);

            ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);

            const angleDeg = parseFloat(angleSlider ? angleSlider.value : 45);
            const v0 = parseFloat(velocitySlider ? velocitySlider.value : 20);
            const g = 9.81;
            const angleRad = (angleDeg * Math.PI) / 180;

            if (angleDisplay) angleDisplay.textContent = `${angleDeg}°`;
            if (velocityDisplay) velocityDisplay.textContent = `${v0} m/s`;

            const maxRange = (Math.pow(v0, 2) * Math.sin(2 * angleRad)) / g;
            const maxHeight = (Math.pow(v0 * Math.sin(angleRad), 2)) / (2 * g);

            if (telemetry) {
                telemetry.textContent = `Range: ${maxRange.toFixed(1)} m | Max Height: ${maxHeight.toFixed(1)} m`;
            }

            // Grid & Axes
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#1E293B';
            ctx.lineWidth = 1;
            for (let x = 30; x < width; x += 40) {
                ctx.beginPath();
                ctx.moveTo(x, 0);
                ctx.lineTo(x, height - 20);
                ctx.stroke();
            }
            for (let y = 20; y < height - 20; y += 30) {
                ctx.beginPath();
                ctx.moveTo(30, y);
                ctx.lineTo(width, y);
                ctx.stroke();
            }

            // Ground
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#475569';
            ctx.lineWidth = 2;
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(30, height - 20);
            ctx.lineTo(width, height - 20);
            ctx.stroke();

            // Parabolic curve
            const scaleX = (width - 50) / 125;
            const scaleY = (height - 40) / 40;

            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#38BDF8';
            ctx.lineWidth = 3;

            const tFlight = (2 * v0 * Math.sin(angleRad)) / g;
            for (let t = 0; t <= tFlight; t += 0.05) {
                const x = v0 * Math.cos(angleRad) * t;
                const y = v0 * Math.sin(angleRad) * t - 0.5 * g * Math.pow(t, 2);

                const canvasX = 30 + x * scaleX;
                const canvasY = (height - 20) - y * scaleY;

                if (t === 0) ctx.moveTo(canvasX, canvasY);
                else ctx.lineTo(canvasX, canvasY);
            }
            ctx.stroke();

            // Impact point
            const endX = 30 + maxRange * scaleX;
            ctx.fillStyle = '#34D399';
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.arc(endX, height - 20, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            ctx.fill();

            // Origin
            ctx.fillStyle = '#60A5FA';
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.arc(30, height - 20, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            ctx.fill();
        }

        angleSlider?.addEventListener('input', drawTrajectory);
        velocitySlider?.addEventListener('input', drawTrajectory);
        window.addEventListener('resize', drawTrajectory);

        // SOCRATIC QUIZ
        const quizButtons = document.querySelectorAll('.quiz-option');
        const feedbackBox = document.getElementById('quiz-feedback');

        quizButtons.forEach(btn => {
            btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
                const choice = btn.getAttribute('data-choice');
                
                quizButtons.forEach(b => {
                    b.classList.remove('border-blue-600', 'bg-blue-50', 'border-emerald-500', 'bg-emerald-50', 'border-amber-500', 'bg-amber-50');
                });

                if (feedbackBox) {
                    feedbackBox.classList.remove('hidden', 'bg-emerald-50', 'border-emerald-200', 'text-emerald-900', 'bg-amber-50', 'border-amber-200', 'text-amber-900');
                    
                    if (choice === 'equal') {
                        btn.classList.add('border-emerald-500', 'bg-emerald-50');
                        feedbackBox.classList.add('bg-emerald-50', 'border-emerald-200', 'text-emerald-900');
                        feedbackBox.innerHTML = `
                            <div class="font-bold flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
                                <i class="fas fa-check-circle text-emerald-600 text-base"></i>
                                <span>Superb Socratic deduction!</span>
                            </div>
                            <p>Exactly: complementary launch angles (30° and 60°) achieve the exact same horizontal range. The reason is trigonometric: sin(2 · 30°) = sin(60°) and sin(2 · 60°) = sin(120°) = sin(60°). One flies higher with lower horizontal velocity, while the other flies low and fast.</p>
                        `;
                    } else {
                        btn.classList.add('border-amber-500', 'bg-amber-50');
                        feedbackBox.classList.add('bg-amber-50', 'border-amber-200', 'text-amber-900');
                        feedbackBox.innerHTML = `
                            <div class="font-bold flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
                                <i class="fas fa-brain text-amber-600 text-base"></i>
                                <span>Socratic hint to reflect:</span>
                            </div>
                            <p>Recall the formula from step 2: X_max = (v_0² · sin(2&alpha;)) / g. What is sin(2 · 30°) = sin(60°)? What is sin(2 · 60°) = sin(120°)? Return to step 2 and adjust the slider between 30° and 60°: where does the green landing point fall?</p>
                        `;
                    }
                }
            });
        });
    </script>

</body>
</html>
